{
  "schemaVersion": "tracy-personalize/v1",
  "note": "What tools/personalize.mjs changes on a customer's copy of the Tracy SaaS template (Kinetic) from their questionnaire answers (seed/questions.json: name / sector / contact). The demo business is Helix Labs, an observability product, and almost everything it says about itself is a CLAIM: named customer logos, 99.99% uptime, 1.2M events/min, three priced tiers, four named founders, quotes from named engineers. None of that is rewritten for the customer - it is REMOVED, because a made-up '99.99% uptime' is a lie in their name. `identity` writes their own words exactly; `replace` swaps the demo brand everywhere; `copy` is prose a model writes for their sector with the demo text as the length reference; `facts` are removed; `hide` unpublishes pages that are nothing but claims. Values use {name} {NAME} {initials} {phone} {address} {year} {sector}.",
  "settings": {
    "title": "{name}"
  },
  "identity": [
    {
      "collection": "social",
      "slug": "footer-brand",
      "field": "brand",
      "value": "{name}"
    },
    {
      "collection": "footerlegal",
      "slug": "footer-copyright",
      "field": "copyright",
      "value": "(c) {year} {name}."
    }
  ],
  "replace": [
    {
      "find": "Helix Labs, Inc.",
      "with": "{name}"
    },
    {
      "find": "Helix Labs",
      "with": "{name}"
    },
    {
      "find": "HELIX",
      "with": "{NAME}"
    },
    {
      "find": "Helix",
      "with": "{name}"
    }
  ],
